  "text": "Maqam Athar Kurd A member of the Maqam Nikriz Family Maqam Index Pronunciation of Athar Kurd Click the notes and hold using the mouse to hear them play. Maqam Athar Kurd is a very rare maqam that seems to be a 20 th century development. Its scale starts with Athar Kurd on the tonic followed by Jins Hijazkar centered around the 5 th degree. The Maqam Athar Kurd scale is a hybrid between Maqam Nawa Athar and Maqam Kurd , hence the name. Explore other maqamat in the Maqam Nikriz Family . Watch a 1-minute sample Violin Taqsim in Maqam Athar Kurd by Sami Abu Shumays. Ya Msafir w Albi Ma‘ak (1950) Leila Murad Music by Ahmad Sidqi el-Hana wel-Widd (1975) Leila Murad Music by Abdel Mun‘im al-Hariri Ya Fagr Nurak Hall w Ban (c.1952) Vocals by Baligh Hamdi Music by Yusef Shawqi el-Hobb Kida (1959) Umm Kulthum Music by Riyad al-Sunbati Sama‘i Hijazkar Kurd Al-Kindi Ensemble The Whirling Dervishes of Damascus Vol. 2 Music by Salah al-Mahdi (Tunisia) Taqsim Oud Riyad al-Sunbati Taqaseem Oud Taqsim Oud Athar Kurd Muhammad Qadri Dalal Maqamat Insolites",
